# P0 and P1 of SAINT-small (CONFIG=saint_reduced, 3.56 M parameters with the head), with the P_v1 recipe
# (rriva, 2026-11-25) shortened to 40 epochs: batch 12800, AdamW lr 1e-3, gradient clip 1.0 (arm=pretrain),
# contrastive T 0.1, noise lambda 0.4, no dropout; WSD: warmup 2 epochs (5 %), constant, linear decay over the last
# 20 % (epochs 32-40); no early stopping, the downstream loads last.ckpt.
#   p1_small = p0 + jet contrastive (weight 1.0, T 0.1) on the aggregator output (the aggregator is trained)
#   p0_small = per-object contrastive on the track and jet-feature embeddings (the aggregator is not trained)
# @est = 6650 s/epoch: model B's P1 on an A40 (148 h for 80 epochs), a deliberate upper bound — SAINT-small was not
# measured before the launch (the measurement job sat in the queue; owner, 2026-11-25).  Its first epoch measures it.
# Seed 42 first, one pretraining per card (a task alone on a card always starts, so no @mem needed):
#   CONFIG=saint_reduced MAX_EPOCHS=40 SEEDS=42 WALLTIME=7-00:00:00 EST_SECONDS_PER_EPOCH=6650 \
#   GPU_NODE=gpu-L40S-open,gpu-A40 STAGE=P_small_s42 PACKS=1 MEM_PER_GPU_GB=24 \
#   CELLS=experiments/2026-11_pretrain-saint-small/configs/P_small.cells bash slurm/ssl_pack.sh
# The other 4 seeds (5 per setting in the end) follow from the measured memory: two per card if a P0 and a P1 fit.
p1_small  arm=pretrain chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12800 optimizer.lr=1e-3 pretrain.loss_weights.jet_contrastive=1.0 optimizer.schedule=wsd optimizer.warmup_epochs=2 optimizer.decay_frac=0.2 ~callbacks.early_stopping @est=6650
p0_small  arm=pretrain chunk_size=512 datamodule.batch_size=12800 optimizer.lr=1e-3 optimizer.schedule=wsd optimizer.warmup_epochs=2 optimizer.decay_frac=0.2 ~callbacks.early_stopping @est=6650
